    "passage": "As the world strives toward a future free of carbon emissions, wind power is arguably one of the most popular alternatives. The cost of generating wind power has come down by almost 40%, thanks to the increasing number of wind turbines worldwide. However, wind turbines may not always [[1]], since they aren’t made for remote locations or deep waters. [[2]] further complicates the matter is that wind turbines aren’t able to reach great heights where the wind is at its strongest and hence where more power can be produced.\nTo [[3]] the growing demands of electricity in as sustainable a way as possible, Mauritius, located off the coast of East Africa, experiments with kites to harvest wind energy. Kites actually have certain [[4]] over conventional wind turbines. Not only can they be installed efficiently and inexpensively, but they are a good fit for a wider range of terrains, locations or environments. They thus hold special appeal for countries with [[5]]. For now, the technique still has a long way to go before large-scale applications become a reality. We will see whether kites can replace wind turbines in the future.",
